WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.650
This is Hotsauce: a free, open source office suite for small teams,

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.430
running on a server you own.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.510
Docs, meetings, tasks, recordings, files and a dozen more apps,

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.810
all in one place, all saved as plain files in Git.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.770
Let's walk through what's in it today.

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:19.638
Every day starts on Today.

00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:22.898
Your next meeting, your tasks, and to-dos pulled from your notes, on one page.

00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:25.758
The sky behind the greeting follows the real time of day,

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.518
with the sun or moon in place.

00:00:28.518 --> 00:00:30.458
Click the weather for the next twelve hours.

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:34.258
Every tile can be moved, added or hidden, so the page fits how you work.

00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:39.518
The rail on the left holds your apps.

00:00:39.518 --> 00:00:41.678
Pin the ones you use, click the logo to see their names,

00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:45.258
and press Command K to jump anywhere or search everything at once.

00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:50.613
Docs are Markdown files, kept in Git.

00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:53.273
Type, and teammates editing beside you show up live.

00:00:53.273 --> 00:00:54.853
Link another doc with two square brackets,

00:00:54.853 --> 00:00:57.653
and the link keeps working even after a rename.

00:00:57.653 --> 00:00:59.693
History shows every version, who changed what,

00:00:59.693 --> 00:01:01.353
and lets you bring any of it back.

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:05.893
Bring in Word, HTML or Markdown files, and download any doc as Word or PDF,

00:01:05.893 --> 00:01:09.033
in your team's own fonts, colours and logo.

00:01:11.865 --> 00:01:13.785
Any doc can become a slide deck.

00:01:13.785 --> 00:01:15.305
Three dashes start a new slide,

00:01:15.305 --> 00:01:18.365
and a line that starts with Notes becomes your speaker notes.

00:01:18.365 --> 00:01:20.985
Present opens the slides full screen, with a laser pointer,

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:24.165
and presenter view shows your notes, the next slide and a timer.

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:30.233
Every doc, meeting note and task has a conversation under it.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:33.293
Type at and a name, and that teammate gets one notification.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.213
Everything you're mentioned in waits in For you, newest first.

00:01:36.213 --> 00:01:38.693
Mark it done, or put it off until tomorrow morning.

00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:44.676
Meetings takes the notes, and no bot joins your call.

00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:47.296
Hotsauce keeps a transcript of who said what, next to your own rough notes.

00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:51.176
When the call ends, it turns both into clean notes from a template you pick,

00:01:51.176 --> 00:01:53.616
with decisions and action items.

00:01:53.616 --> 00:01:54.636
Meetings come from your calendar,

00:01:54.636 --> 00:01:58.156
and booking links let people outside the team pick a time.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.940
Ask a question across every meeting and doc,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:05.460
and the answer points back to its sources, so you can check it.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.800
Hotsauce also keeps a short brief for each person, of what they're working on,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.320
so your AI tools start already knowing the context.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.320
Claude, ChatGPT and others can connect to Hotsauce and work as you.

00:02:17.607 --> 00:02:19.707
Action items land in Tasks.

00:02:19.707 --> 00:02:23.127
Type a task in plain words, and the date fills itself in.

00:02:23.127 --> 00:02:24.947
Tasks can repeat and remind you.

00:02:24.947 --> 00:02:27.507
Or press Ramble and just talk for a few seconds,

00:02:27.507 --> 00:02:30.067
and Hotsauce sorts what you said into a clean list.

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:35.082
Notes hold the small stuff.

00:02:35.082 --> 00:02:38.442
Colour them, pin them, label them, or turn one into a checklist.

00:02:42.021 --> 00:02:43.581
Check-ins ask the team a question on a schedule,

00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:45.681
like what will you get done this week?

00:02:45.681 --> 00:02:47.101
Everyone's answers gather in one place,

00:02:47.101 --> 00:02:49.501
and a short summary posts to your team chat.

00:02:52.987 --> 00:02:55.387
Clips replaces the meeting you didn't need.

00:02:55.387 --> 00:02:58.127
Record your screen with your camera in the corner and talk it through.

00:02:58.127 --> 00:03:00.607
Trim the ends, and whoever watches gets a transcript,

00:03:00.607 --> 00:03:04.247
a summary and the action items, at whatever speed they like.

00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:06.367
Share a link with people outside the team.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.709
Dictate turns talking into clean text.

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:14.409
On the Mac, hold a key, talk, and let go.

00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:18.129
The words land wherever your cursor is, in any app, with the ums taken out.

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:21.009
Pick how much clean-up you want, and keep it all on your Mac if you'd rather.

00:03:21.009 --> 00:03:23.109
It even works with no internet connection.

00:03:24.676 --> 00:03:28.636
The Mac app sets itself up in four steps: your workspace, signing in,

00:03:28.636 --> 00:03:31.236
a quick try of Dictate, and the permissions it needs,

00:03:31.236 --> 00:03:32.436
each with a plain reason.

00:03:32.436 --> 00:03:35.936
Once it's running, it notices when a call starts and offers to take notes,

00:03:35.936 --> 00:03:37.816
takes screenshots you can mark up and share,

00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:39.756
and updates itself with one click.

00:03:40.243 --> 00:03:41.303
Not on a Mac?

00:03:41.303 --> 00:03:44.603
The Chrome extension takes notes on Google Meet calls right in the browser,

00:03:44.603 --> 00:03:45.603
without Chrome's share-your-tab dialog.

00:03:45.603 --> 00:03:48.063
It connects to your Hotsauce in one click,

00:03:48.063 --> 00:03:51.163
and its setup page walks you through pinning it and trying a test call.

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:54.463
It also saves any page to Links in one click.

00:03:56.743 --> 00:03:57.743
Links is your read-later list.

00:03:57.743 --> 00:04:00.603
Save from the extension, your phone or the app,

00:04:00.603 --> 00:04:02.643
and read a clean copy without the clutter.

00:04:02.643 --> 00:04:06.323
Highlight passages and add notes, and Hotsauce remembers where you stopped.

00:04:06.323 --> 00:04:08.563
Research papers come with their authors and abstract.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:15.612
Files holds the team's uploads, with previews and search.

00:04:15.612 --> 00:04:19.752
PDFs come with tools: combine and reorder pages, split, shrink for email,

00:04:19.752 --> 00:04:22.572
make a scanned page searchable, or black out a name for good.

00:04:22.572 --> 00:04:24.052
The original never changes.

00:04:24.052 --> 00:04:25.832
You get a new PDF beside it.

00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:30.339
Need a signature?

00:04:30.339 --> 00:04:33.419
Pick a PDF, list who signs, and place their fields.

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:35.799
Each person gets their own link, no account needed.

00:04:35.799 --> 00:04:38.479
You can follow who has signed, and when the last one does,

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:42.599
a sealed copy with its audit certificate lands in Files and goes to everyone.

00:04:46.376 --> 00:04:48.796
Forms collect surveys, sign-ups and requests,

00:04:48.796 --> 00:04:51.696
from the team or anyone with the link.

00:04:51.696 --> 00:04:54.156
Tables are trackers with real spreadsheet formulas,

00:04:54.156 --> 00:04:56.376
kept as simple files you can open anywhere.

00:05:02.898 --> 00:05:05.618
Boards are hand-drawn whiteboards the whole team can sketch on at once.

00:05:05.618 --> 00:05:09.078
People is everyone you meet with, filled in from your calendar,

00:05:09.078 --> 00:05:11.038
with a short note about each.

00:05:12.731 --> 00:05:16.111
And Briefcast is a five-minute spoken briefing every weekday morning,

00:05:16.111 --> 00:05:20.631
from your meetings, tasks and reading, ready to play in any podcast app.

00:05:23.745 --> 00:05:24.785
Hotsauce bends to fit you.

00:05:24.785 --> 00:05:28.925
Describe a look, like a warm forest cabin, and the whole app previews it.

00:05:28.925 --> 00:05:31.185
Turn on soft background music while you work,

00:05:31.185 --> 00:05:34.485
or screen breaks that remind you to look away every twenty minutes.

00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:38.205
And if something's wrong or you have an idea, send feedback from any page,

00:05:38.205 --> 00:05:40.565
with a picture of what you were looking at.

00:05:42.245 --> 00:05:44.285
Hotsauce is free and open source.

00:05:44.285 --> 00:05:46.905
It deploys to Cloudflare or your own server in minutes,

00:05:46.905 --> 00:05:50.085
backs itself up every night, keeps working when the connection drops,

00:05:50.085 --> 00:05:51.205
and updates itself.

00:05:51.205 --> 00:05:53.425
Your work stays in plain files you own.

00:05:53.425 --> 00:05:56.245
Try the live demo, or get it at hotsauce.work.
